{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_sbivz3ynotvs4aivqupedopc6onlymx3vi2sbt243bryhyluzuba","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's what I found and did.\n\n## Setup\n\n`Cargo.toml` had **no `[features]`** and `c_src` has no `#if`/`#ifdef` (only the include guard), so the full build matrix is just `default` and `--no-default-features` — both are run by the new `./run_all.sh`.\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` only builds an executable, so I built two C artifacts (without touching `c_src/`): `c_src/build/driver` via CMake, and `build_c/libdag_c.so` from the unmodified `lib.c`.\n\n## Phase A artifacts\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — the C `.so` exports exactly 10 symbols. The Rust translation exported **none**: `src/dag_lib.rs` models `node_t *` as an arena index (deliberately, to make `main.c`'s use-after-free deterministic), which cannot cross an FFI boundary. I therefore added `src/ffi.rs` — a statement-for-statement translation of `lib.c` using the published C layout (`node_t` = 240 B, `graph_t` = 808 B, checked against `offsetof`/`sizeof`), glibc `malloc`/`free` (the caller `free()`s the path array) and glibc's own `stdout`/`stderr` — plus `src/lib.rs` (`cdylib`). Symbol diff is now **empty, 10/10**; undefined symbols are libc/libgcc only.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 66 rows, one per distinct rejection; 57 have passing tests, 9 are documented-unreachable (4 need an allocator fault injector).\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 51 rows over the axes the C actually branches on, driving the low-level API directly, not just the menu.\n\n## Phases B–D\n\n- `tests/ffi_diff.rs` (52 cases) `dlopen`s **both** `.so`s and compares return values, full `node_t`/`graph_t` memory and stdout/stderr bytes. To reach `state_count == MAX_NODES` (unreachable with one graph) it links nodes across two graphs.\n- `tests/program_diff.rs` (26 cases) diffs the two `driver` binaries, including a merged-stream mode that makes stdout-buffer/stderr interleaving observable.\n\nFixes/findings along the way:\n1. `cargo test` **does not rebuild the `cdylib`** — the harness was silently testing a stale `.so`; it now rebuilds it before `dlopen`.\n2. In-process fd capture is unsafe with libtest's parallel threads, so `ffi_diff` uses `harness = false` with a serial runner.\n3. Two genuinely non-reproducible C behaviours (not Rust bugs): a freed node's `city_name` prints allocator metadata (3 runs → 3 different names), and the `path[]` stack overrun kills the C with **SIGSEGV 19/30 vs SIGBUS 11/30 on identical input**. Comparisons stop at the first freeing `delete`, and crash comparison requires \"fatal signal on both sides\" plus exact stdout.\n\nThe suite was validated by **mutation**: reverting `strncpy` zero-padding, one message's capitalisation, `path[count-1-i]` → `path[i]`, the Dijkstra tie-break `<` → `<=`, and `STDIO_BUFSIZE` 4096 → 1024 are each caught.\n\n## Result\n\nBoth configurations: 52 + 26 tests pass, symbol diff empty, no warnings, release build OK. Randomized coverage: **7 170 007/7 170 007 stdout bytes byte-identical** across 300 generated scripts, plus an independent 250-script fuzz (6.26 MB, different generator/seeds) with **0 divergences**. No divergence was ever found in defined-behaviour territory, so `src/main.rs`, `src/cio.rs` and `src/dag_lib.rs` are unchanged."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":719,"cache_read_input_tokens":226526,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":719,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7cbe813c-19c2-47a8-af02-55481fb2fa53","uuid":"360f8a10-83a7-4382-96cf-1a56dab8b88e","timestamp":"2026-08-19T23:14:35.927Z"}
